  "notes": "{憎|にく}む is transitive (⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧). It takes ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ for the object of hatred.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{憎|にく}んで⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates an ongoing state of hatred.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{憎|にく}む (to hate someone)\n- ⟦{罪|つみ}→罪：03532_tsumi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{憎|にく}む (to hate sin/crime)\n- {憎|にく}んで⟦も→も：00484_mo⟧{憎|にく}みきれない (to hate but not be able to hate enough)\n- ～⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{憎|にく}む: The object of hatred\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{憎|にく}い→憎い：12744_nikui⟧: I-adjective meaning \"hateful\" or (sarcastically) \"admirably skilled\"\n- ⟦{憎|にく}しみ→憎しみ：15769_nikushimi⟧: Noun meaning \"hatred\"\n- ⟦{恨|うら}む→恨む：00415_uramu⟧: To resent, bear a grudge (similar but with nuance of resentment)\n\nRegister: Neutral. A strong word expressing deep negative emotion.",
